  "reading": {
   "title": "Emre's birthday dinner",
   "text": "On Friday night, Hafsa and Emre go to a small restaurant downtown. It is Emre's birthday. The waiter brings the menu. Emre is very hungry. \"I'll have the chicken soup and a big salad,\" he says. Hafsa looks at the menu for a long time. \"I'll have fish, please,\" she says. The waiter smiles. \"Of course. And what will you drink?\" \"Water for me,\" says Emre. \"I'll have tea,\" says Hafsa.\n\nAfter dinner, the waiter asks, \"Will you have dessert?\" Emre says yes. \"We'll share a chocolate cake,\" Hafsa says. When the bill comes, Emre tries to pay, but Hafsa says, \"No, no. It's your birthday. I will pay. I'll also leave a good tip.\" Emre smiles. \"Thank you, Mom. I promise I'll pay next time.\"",
   "glossary": [
    {
     "en": "birthday",
     "tr": "doğum günü"
